ng Houston, Corpus Christi, Beaumont, and others out of the equation altogether with them receiving little or no funding to serve the Black and Brown communities.\par \par \uc2 H.U.D. found in an investigation race and national origin discrimination and we agree.\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: Now the Washington -- let me go to "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " and let me go to this -- we`re following breaking news out of Buffalo. Police in Buffalo holding a news conference right now, let`s listen in.\par \par \uc2 MAYOR BYRON BROWN, BUFFALO, NEW YORK: Okay, I know, this is tight quarters. Ellen, let me know when we`re good.\par \par \uc2 What started out as a beautiful day in the City of Buffalo has turned into a terrible day and one of tremendous heartbreak for me every member of our community, we have suffered a mass shooting with multiple casualties and several people injured.\par \par \uc2 [17:45:08]\par \par \uc2 BROWN: This is the worst nightmare that any community can face, and we are hurting and we are seething right now as a community.\par \par \uc2 The depth of pain that families are feeling, and that all of us are feeling right now cannot even be explained. Some of us had the opportunity to provide comfort to some of the families. But needless to say, there is no comfort at this time.\par \par \uc2 We are pleased that a shooter is in custody. The person responsible for the tragic events of today is in custody. You will get more details in a moment.\par \par \uc2 I want to thank all of the law enforcement agencies at the Federal, state, county and city level, all of the agencies that have responded. Buffalo is known as the City of good neighbors, nationally and internationally. This is a community where people love each other.\par \par \uc2 The shooter was not from this community. In fact, the shooter traveled hours from outside this community to perpetrate this crime on the people of Buffalo, a day when people were enjoying the sunshine, enjoying family, enjoying friends, all manner of happy activities. People in a supermarket shopping, and bullets raining down on them. People`s lives being snuffed out in an instant, for no reason.\par \par \uc2 I have to say that this particular Top supermarket is near and dear to my heart. It`s one that I worked years ago to help bring to this community. It`s one that I patronize from time to time, my family patronizes from time to time, and some of the victims of this shooter`s attack are people that all of us standing up here know. So this is a day of great pain for our community.\par \par \uc2 I want to just recognize some of those that are with us today before I turn things over to our Police Commissioner Joseph Gramaglia to give you more detail. I want to recognize County Executive, \uc2 Mark Poloncarz\uc2 , Erie County Executive, Congressman \uc2 Brian Higgins\uc2 . Council President -- Buffalo City Council President Darius Pridgen, Erie County Legislature Chairwoman April Baskin, Erie County legislator Howard Johnson.\par \par \uc2 I want to recognize Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  and thank her for her calls. Governor`s staff is with us now and the Governor is flying back into town and will be here sometime after seven o`clock.\par \par \uc2 I want to recognize Attorney General Letitia James, who has also called and we have also received calls from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Again, this is a day of great sadness for all of us in the City of Buffalo.\par \par \uc2 To provide you with more detail, I want to turn things over to Buffalo Police Commissioner Joseph Gramaglia.\par \par \uc2 COMMISSIONER JOSEPH GRAMAGLIA, BUFFALO POLICE: Thank you, Mayor.\par \par \uc2 At approximately 2:30 today, an individual who as the Mayor stated is not from this area and is from hours away, drove to Buffalo, went to 1275 Jefferson Avenue to the Tops Market. He exited his vehicle. He was very heavily armed. He had tactical gear. He had a tactical helmet on. He had a camera that he was live streaming what he was doing.\par \par \uc2 The individual exited his car and engaged four individuals. He shot four people in the parking lot. Three of those were deceased. One individual at this time is surviving the injury.\par \par \uc2 The individual went inside. As I said, he is an 18-year-old White male, walked into the store and began engaging customers inside the store. One of the individuals inside the store is a security guard, a beloved security guard, who is a retired Buffalo Police officer, a hero in our eyes, engaged the suspect, fired multiple shots, struck the suspect, but because he had heavily armored plating on, that bullet had no round, the suspects engaged our retired officer and he was ultimately shot and deceased at the scene.\par \par \uc2 [17:55:20]\par \par \uc2 GRAMAGLIA: He continued to work his way through the store. Ultimately, he worked his way back towards the front of the store. Buffalo Police immediately responded and engaged the suspect in the vestibule of the store, and at that point, the suspect put the gun to his own neck. Buffalo Police personnel, two patrol officers talked the suspect into dropping the gun. He dropped the gun, took off some of his tactical gear, surrendered at that point and he was led outside, put in a police car and transported to the Buffalo Police Headquarters.\par \par \uc2 So as we said, a total of 13 people were shot today, 10 deceased at the scene and three sustained nonlife threatening injuries that appears to be nonlife threatening injuries at that point. Four in total were store employees. One of those was the security guard who has worked at that location for a very long time.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, many officers on scene here, knew him quite well and the rest of the victims are customers of the store.\par \par \uc2 You know, as the Mayor said, this tragic incident by someone who is not a part of our community, does not live here. We`ll let some of the other agencies get into the information that has been posted online. And I will turn this over at this point first to our Erie County Sheriff John Garcia.\par \par \uc2 I would like to thank all of the agencies. We have a very, very close working relationship with every level of government, every level of law enforcement, and everybody was immediately calling and responding. We had a command post set up and everybody is asking what we can do and how can we pitch in.\par \par \uc2 The individuals from several hours away, the New York State Police and the F.B.I. are investigating that part of the crime as well. So, I will turn this over at this point to Erie County Sheriff, John Garcia.\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF JOHN GARCIA, ERIE COUNTY SHERIFF: Thank you, Commissioner Gramaglia.\par \par \uc2 As your Sheriff and on behalf of the men and women of the Erie County Sheriff`s Office, our condolences to the victims and their families. From law enforcement standpoint, the Erie County Sheriff`s Office responded, boots on the ground Deputies, investigators, our helicopter in the air, our SWAT team on standby, and as Commissioner Gramaglia said, we are working together every single day to keep the community safe.\par \par \uc2 This was pure evil. It was straight up racially motivated hate crime from somebody outside of our community, outside of the city of good neighbors, as the Mayor said, coming into our community and trying to inflict that evil upon us.\par \par \uc2 I urge everyone to stay calm, and we are there to protect the citizens of Erie County and Buffalo and we will be out there along with the City of Buffalo Police Department patrolling.\par \par \uc2 And, again, my condolences to the family. And this person was a pure evil.\par \par \uc2 So thank you.\par \par \uc2 STEVEN BELANGER, SPECIAL AGENT IN CHARGE OF F.B.I. BUFFALO FIELD OFFICE: I`m Steven Belanger. I`m the Special Agent in charge of the F.B.I.`s Buffalo field office.\par \par \uc2 We stand here today confronted with feelings of anger, shock, confusion, fear and compassion.\par \par \uc2 We feel motivated to help and relieve the anguish of those who were killed and injured today and their families and friends.\par \par \uc2 These victims did not deserve this. They were doing what we do every day, going to the grocery store or simply doing our jobs. The F.B.I. is working this case jointly with our partners with the Buffalo PD and our other Federal, state and local partners.\par \par \uc2 We are investigating this incident as both a hate crime and a case of racially motivated violent extremism.\par \par \uc2 Hate crimes fall within the F.B.I.`s Criminal Investigative Division and racially motivated violent extremism cases fall within the F.B.I.`s Counterterrorism Division within our Domestic Terrorism Section.\par \par \uc2 The F.B.I. is providing all necessary resources, both locally and nationally to investigate this matter. We will not stop until every lead is investigated, every piece of evidence is analyzed, and until we understand how and why this horrible tragedy and crime occurred.\par \par \uc2 Our thoughts and our prayers are with the family and the victims who died today.\par \par \uc2 [18:00:06]\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED. END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 MSNBC.  ALL RIGHTS  RESERVED.  Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the  prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You may not alter  or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the  content. \par \par \uc2 Document MSLIV00020220515ei5e00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 THE LAST WORD WITH LAWRENCE O`DONNELL for May 13, 2022, MSNBC\b0\par\par\uc2 Ali Velshi, Jonathan Capehart, David Jolly, Cal Perry, Rick 