r \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: And do you think that Russian listeners are listening for that? Even if they initially supported what they thought \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  was trying to do in Ukraine?\par \par \uc2 At this point, would at least some Russian listeners be able to comprehend that this isn`t going the way he wants to?\par \par \uc2 ROTHKOPF: Well, of course, both you and I are old enough to remember when Kremlin-ology was a big thing. People would watch who was standing next to the Soviet leader to see who is in favor and who was not.\par \par \uc2 And of course, they know there`s a war going on. And they listened for clues in what Putin was saying as to whether they were doing well or on.\par \par \uc2 But in the past few days, he`s been forced to acknowledge the losses. He is actually set up programs to remunerate families for the losses of soldiers who have died there. And he seemed very flat, very lackluster. And so, within Russia. You have people getting the clues that this is not going well.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: David Rothkopf, thank you for joining us and thank you for watching \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  for us. Thank you very much, David.\par \par \uc2 ROTHKOPF: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 [22:54:53]\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: Time for tonight`s LAST WORD --\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. KEVIN MCCARTHY (R-CA), HOUSE MINORITY LEADER: The president bears responsibility for Wednesday`s attack on Congress by mob rioters.\par \par \uc2 [22:59:50]\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MITCH MCCONNELL\uc2  (R-KY): There is no question, none that President Trump is practically and morally responsible for provoking the events of the day.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: And those are tonight`s unforgettable LAST WORDs.\par \par \uc2 "THE 11TH HOUR WITH STEPHANIE RUHLE" starts now.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 MSNBC.  A