ould be key to Senate control for Republicans or for Democrats in November.\par \par \uc2 The former president was on the ground in western PA this weekend where the rainy Friday night rally backing Mehmet Oz in the Republican Senate primary, while hammering Oz`s chief GOP rival David McCormick. We`ll have more on that fight in just a minute.\par \par \uc2 Trump hasn`t endorsed in the state`s other marquee contests this year. That`s the governor`s race, but whoever he picks will likely square off in November with Democratic AG \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How the political winds are shifting in Pennsylvania politics is going to reverberate through Washington in the midterms and probably right into 2024 as well which is why Chuck is hitting the road for two days of special "Meet the Midterms" coverage on the ground in Pennsylvania right here on MEET THE PRESS DAILY. That starts tomorrow. He`ll be speaking with voters, officials, candidates and a lot more. Be sure to tune in, politics and gas stations sandwiches are included, I`m told. That`s exciting.\par \par \uc2 My political panel joins me here on set after this short break. Stick around.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:45:20]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT: Dr. Oz is a man who truly believes in Make America Great Again or the MAGA movement. He believes it 100 percent. And he is in love with our country. Dr. Oz is running against the liberal Wall Street Republican named David McCormick who I`ve known. He may be a nice guy, but he`s not MAGA. He`s not MAGA. He`s more Toomey than he is MAGA.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HAAKE: Welcome back. That`s former President Trump`s view on the Republican Senate primary in Pennsylvania. Mehmet Oz is MAGA, Dave McCormick Toomey than MAGA. The Trump bump was enough to propel a celebrity candidate out of a crowded field in neighboring Ohio, but will Pennsylvania now be a different story?\par \par \uc2 Joining me now on set is Jake Sherman, co-founder of "Punch Bowl News" and an MSNBC contributor, Democratic strategist Juanita Tolliver, she`s also an MSNBC political analyst, and Matthew Continetti, senior fellow at the \uc2 American Enterprise Institute\uc2  and author of the new book "The Right: The Hundred Year War for American Conservatism."\par \par \uc2 So, Jake, let`s pick up right there. I mean, the Pennsylvania primary, is this another place where we will see Donald Trump`s strategy of endorse the most famous guy in the race pay off? How is this similar? How`s it different from what we saw in Ohio?\par \par \uc2 JAKE SHERMAN, PUNCHBOWL NEWS CO-FOUNDER: It`s a good question. I mean I think there`s polling today that has shown that Oz is in the lead, but not by that much, with 15 percent undecided, which to me at this point in the race seems quite high. I mean, 15 percent undecided, you have to assume that that is going to sway the race in a one or two-point race. By the way, between first and third, not only between first and second, but three candidates in the mix there.\par \par \uc2 HAAKE: Right. It`s a total food fight. And Matt, David McCormick is not taking this lying down. I want to play for you how he responded to the president. Take a listen to this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DAVID MCCORMICK\uc2 , FORMER BRIDGEWATER ASSOCIATES CEO: I`m running on President Trump`s Great America First agenda. I think President Trump did a great job for Pennsylvania. And I`m running as the person who is battle tested and Pennsylvania true and can actually win this primary, win this race. It`s going to be the biggest Senate race in history.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HAAKE: So does it matter who the ultimate arbiter of who MAGA is? I mean, what do you make of the pushback there from McCormick?\par \par \uc2 MATTHEW CONTINETTI, AMERICAN ENTERPRISE INSTITUTE SENIOR FELLOW: I think Trump is the arbiter of what MAGA 