cally correcting the disparities between basically cocaine and crack and some other things that they`re preparing to basically be responsive to their base.\par \par \uc2 So, it will be interesting to see what they pull out of their hat, but it is important that the economy is also doing pretty well, Rev, with jobs actually on the uptick. I think that everyone is concerned about the possibility of inflation and perhaps a recession, but, still, you know the economy and jobs is looking pretty good right now considering everything we have been through as a nation.\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: Same question to you, Rick. What would Republicans need to do to appeal to black voters? This same \uc2 New York Times\uc2  piece said they were beginning to try and pick up some black voters. What do they need to do given their record and given how some have come off and, in my judgment, as openly hostile to the interest of black voters?\par \par \uc2 TYLER: Well, I think the way appeal to black voters is an economic appeal. And, you know, it is true the economy is booming.\par \par \uc2 [17:35:02]\par \par \uc2 The economy is doing very, very well. But what`s hurting people now, even though they have jobs and wages have gone up, is inflation.\par \par \uc2 And the administration poured a lot of money into the economy and it created an inflation that is hitting food prices and gas prices and energy prices in particular, and the administration needs to address that because it`s just gouging people`s paychecks. They don`t feel like they may be ahead on paper but they don`t feel like they`re ahead when they`re actually behind because things are costing so much more than they did before.\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: Rick. Let`s turn to the looming case of uptick in cases as the COVID variant BA.2 proves to be more contagious than omicron. Dr. Fauci said this morning, the virus won`t be eradicated or eliminated, and it`s up to individuals to make their own medical risk assessments for them and t