as any because I don`t think he really cares.\par \par \uc2 But it is a very serious issue when we have the wife of a Supreme Court justice who has access to, for example, a lister (ph), basically a group chat of all of \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 ` law clerks. You know, these are law clerks, current law clerks. This is very concerning and he absolutely should be recusing himself. Whether or not Ginni Thomas is completely independent from \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , it is impossible for the American public to believe that \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  can he can be impartial in any case, in which his wife has interest, and on that basis alone, he should be recusing himself.\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: Imani, let`s look ahead for a moment. There are still two and a half years to go in President Biden`s term, so it`s certainly possible he could see another vacancy open in the Supreme Court. Now, that Biden has fulfilled his promise to a black woman in terms of putting one on the court, the highest bench in the land, are there other ways that he could potentially broaden the prospective of the court?\par \par \uc2 GANDY: I mean, Biden has been doing a really great job of diversifying the courts. He`s appointed something like 33 or 35 black women to circuit courts around the country. The problem is and the problem remains, until we have broad court reform, that conservatives spent decades packing these courts. One of four appellate judges is a Trump appointed judge. So, these are people who are going to have essentially the last say when it comes to any sort of progressive policy that Biden might want to get through.\par \par \uc2 So, until he`s willing to think about broad court reform, a lot of his efforts are certainly -- they`re wonderful and they`re admirable but, ultimately, it`s just not enough. And I wish that he would do more, but he`s indicated that he`s not really willing to go there, and I think that`s very unfortunate.\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: All right. Well, let me thank you, Imani Gandy, for being with us this evening.\par \par \uc2 Up next, my final thoughts. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [17:50:00]\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: As we continue to cover the war in Ukraine and the historic confirmation of Judge \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 , I want to highlight some other important stories so they don`t get lost in the fog of war.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors in Minnesota announced this week they will not file criminal charges against the Minneapolis officer who shot and killed 22-year-old Amir Locke earlier this year during a no-knock raid. Minnesota A.G. Keith Ellison and Hennepin county attorney Michael Friedman said in a statement there was, quote, insufficient, admissible evidence to file charges.\par \par \uc2 Karen Wells, the mother of Amir Locke, spoke at a press conference at the National Action Network convention on Wednesday, the day they announced it, and expressed her frustrations with the decision.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court reinstated a Trump-era rule limiting the ability for states and Native American tribes to block pipelines and energy projects on their land.\par \par \uc2 [17:55:11]\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is working on a rewrite of the rule. However, the final version won`t be ready until the spring of next year. And two \uc2 NFL\uc2  coaches have joined Brian Flores in the class action lawsuit accusing the league of racial discrimination over its hiring practices. This comes as it was announced last week that the league is required to hire an offensive coach who is a person of ethnic or racial minority or a female in the next season.\par \par \uc2 These are things that came out of National Action Network`s convention, some of these stories. We are focused on protecting rights to vote, fighting on the ground in these states some of the laws that are restrictive and getting people out to vote.\par \par \uc2 Secondly, we are absolutely going to deal with criminal just