ase promise me you`ll come back. We would love to have you back on the show.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I will be back anytime. Thank you so much for having me. I appreciate you guys. Peace and love.\par \par \uc2 REID: Thank you. Peace and love. Cheers. OK, that is tonight`s "REIDOUT." What a wonderful kid. ALL IN WITH CHRIS HAYES starts now.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHRIS HAYES, MSNBC HOST (voiceover): Tonight on ALL IN. \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 . enters the coup-plotting storyline. Tonight, new reporting Don Jr. list of ways to stop Joe Biden`s certification, including his texts to \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  that "We have operational control to do it." And why the January 6 committee now believes the Capitol attack included a coordinated assault by the Oath Keepers and Proud Boy.\par \par \uc2 Then stunning evidence of what looks like a deliberate attack on a known evacuation site in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 And as a country brown Jackson era dawns, David Plouffe on what Democrats can do to counter an out of control conservative court. When ALL IN starts right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HAYES (on camera): Good evening from New York. I`m Chris Hayes. The insurrection of January 6 was not a spur-of-the-moment event. The crowd did not go nuts in the heat of the moment. The rioters were not whipped up into a violent mob just on that day. No. The insurrection was incited over a period of several months, beginning even before the election, and continuing all the way through to January 6.\par \par \uc2 We know that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and many of his allies were involved in building that incitement, from Jeffrey Clark, he`s the lawyer at the Department of Justice, Trump`s own personal lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  who were pushing election fraud conspiracies, to \uc2 John Eastman\uc2  who wrote the now-infamous memo on how to actually execute the coup.\par \par \uc2 Well, today, we are learning new details about the involvement of the ex- President`s own son. We already knew that Don Jr. texted his father`s Chief of Staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  while the insurrection was happening, pleading with him to stop it. "He`s got to condemn this ASAP. \uc2 The Capitol Police\uc2  tweet is not enough." And "We need an Oval Office address. He has to lead now. It has gone too far and gotten out of hand."\par \par \uc2 We are learning though that Don Jr. was texting \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  "ideas for overturning the 2020 election before it was even called" according to CNN. The message is from November 5, just two days after the election and it is among the texts Meadows turned over the January 6 Committee.\par \par \uc2 In it, Trump Jr. lays out ideas for keeping his father in power by subverting the Electoral College process. Writing, "It`s very simple. We have multiple paths. We control them all." He goes on, "To outline a strategy that is nearly identical to what allies of the former president like \uc2 John Eastman\uc2  and \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , and Jeffrey Clark actually attempted to carry out in the months that follow.\par \par \uc2 He talks about filing lawsuits and advocating recounts to prevent certain swing states from certifying the results, as well as having a handful of Republican state houses put forward slates of fake Trump electors. If all that failed, Republican lawmakers in Congress could simply vote to reinstall Trump as president on January 6.\par \par \uc2 "Republicans control 28 steps -- states, Democrats 22 states, once again Trump wins. We either have a vote we control and we win or it gets kicked to Congress January 6, 2021. We have operational control, total leverage, moral high ground. POTUS must start second term now."\par \par \uc2 Wow. They just wrote it all down, didn`t they? So, the ex-President`s son was stirring up plans for overturn the election, building the case for the instruction before all the votes were even counted, before it was called. And in the following days and weeks, Trump and his allies continued exactly that plan inciting what happened on January 6.\par \par \uc2 For example, one of the members of the mob confirmed that in his interview with the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , QAnon follower Douglas Jensen seen here on January 6 told the \uc2 FBI\uc2  that he was influenced by the ex-President`s lawyers. I quote him here. Lin Wood got me fired up. \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2  got me fired up. \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  got me fired up. Yes, they were firing people up.\par \par \uc2 Trump`s lawyers following the ideas laid out by Don Jr. on November 5 incited Doug Jensen to go to the Capitol on January 6 where he broke into the building and infamously chased Officer Eugene Goodman up the stairs in this now-infamous footage from that day. Jensen is now trying to suppress that interview that he voluntarily gave the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , perhaps regretting that he opened his mouth.\par \par \uc2 The way that I`ve come to see it is that there were basically kind of three buckets, three categories of people involved with the insurrection, and they`re all part of one story. There is, of course, the ex-president, his inner circle of enablers. Then there`s the mob who answered the call to action. And then there`s this middle category that sort of knits the two together.\par \par \uc2 That`s the key one in some ways. They`re the foot soldiers, the far-right dress-up militias. This includes the Oath Keepers, a group of whom you see here maneuvering up the Capitol steps in an organized formation, as well as the Proud Boys, the Three Percenters. They`re the ones who basically took orders from on high and executed them on the ground. They plan, they plotted, they organized in the weeks leading up to and on the day, and then carried out an invasion of the United States Capitol.\par \par \uc2 [20:05:27]\par \par \uc2 Now, we`ve learned bits and pieces about their role on January 6. The indictment of several Oath Keepers for seditious conspiracy revea