bering \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as president, even Republicans who say they like him, even Republicans who believe the election was stolen from him, he`s becoming less appealing as a national candidate.\par \par \uc2 TODD: Let me ask you this, Brian Todd. Do you think there`s a scenario where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loses the midterms and Republicans win the midterms? Very quick.\par \par \uc2 B. TODD: This year -- no, I don`t think any election is ever about a former president. Popular or non-popular.\par \par \uc2 TODD: Right. But he could have a bad midterm and that could end the start of the beginning of the --\par \par \uc2 B. TODD: I don`t think there is such a thing. There are two political parties. The Republicans are going to win the majority or Democrats are going to win the majority. I think we don`t have elections about former presidents. It`s just not done.\par \par \uc2 TODD: All right. I got to leave it there because I`m at the end of my clock.\par \par \uc2 Amy, Brad, Jeh, thank you all.\par \par \uc2 We`ll be back with more MEET THE PRESS tomorrow. MSNBC`s coverage will continue with Katy Tur after the break.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED. END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 MSNBC.  ALL RIGHTS  RESERVED.  Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the  prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You may not alter  or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the  content. \par \par \uc2 Document MSNMPD0020220331ei3u00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 THE RACHEL MADDOW SHOW for March 22, 2022, MSNBC\b0\par\par\uc2 Ali Velshi, Gabe Gutierrez, Ali Arouzi \par \uc2 7,942 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2022\par \uc2 MS