par \par \uc2 What message do you think this sends to girls, who aspire to compete and win in sports at the highest levels?\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Senator, I`m not sure what message that sense, if you`re asking me about the legal messages associated with, it those are topics that are being hotly discussed, as you say, and could come to the court. So I`m unable to --\par \par \uc2 BLACKBURN: I think it tells other girls that their voices don`t matter. I think it tells them that they are second-class citizens. And parents want to have a Supreme Court justice who is committed to preserving parental autonomy, and protecting our nations children.\par \par \uc2 So, I -- let`s move on, I want to go to the child porn issue. I know that it`s -- we discuss this today on several different times, what is troubled to me is your consistent pattern of sentencing these predators below these sentences recommended by the government, and the sentencing guidelines. Senator Cruz, Senator Hawley --\par \par \uc2 VELSHI: Senator Marshall Blackburn of Tennessee is questioning Judge \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  as part of the two of the hearings, which are not over yet. They still continue.\par \par \uc2 We have been listening to some of the unusual line of questioning today, this isn`t really questioning. Senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  was asking Judge Jackson whether or not she can define what a woman is. There`s been a lot of concentration on transgender people, students. There`s been lots of attention to critical race theory and matters like that, that is more of what we can expect this evening as it continues and tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 But for now, that does it for us. We are going to see you again tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 But it`s time to hand it over to Lawrence O`Donnell for "THE LAST WORD".\par \par \uc2 Good evening, Lawrence.\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED. END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyrig